.TH FKSTRWRITE 3 2026-09-24 "fkstring" "fkstring Library Manual"
.nh
.SH NAME
fkstrwrite \- write an fkstring to a file descriptor
.SH LIBRARY
fkstring library
.RI ( libfkstring ,\~ \-lfkstring )
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <fkstring.h>
.PP
.BI "ssize_t fkstrwrite(int " fd ", const fkstring *" fks );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR fkstrwrite ()
writes the contents of
.IR fks ,
including any embedded NUL bytes, to the file descriptor
.I fd
with a single call to
.BR write (2).
If
.I fks
is NULL or empty, it makes a zero-length
.BR write (2).
.SH RETURN VALUE
The return value of
.BR write (2):
the number of bytes written, or \-1 with
.I errno
set.
.SH ERRORS
See
.BR write (2).
.SH NOTES
Like
.BR write (2),
.BR fkstrwrite ()
may write fewer bytes than
.BR fkstrlen ( fks ),
for example to a pipe or socket, or when interrupted by a signal.
It does not retry.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR write (2),
.BR fkstring (3),
.BR fkstrread (3),
.BR fkcat (3)
